    {
      "id": "claim_95a1672f2049439dbcf34c6748a0994b",
      "statement": "Codependix deliberately duplicates ESLint's 32 depConstraints as boundary rules because codependix reads the Nx project graph (seeing implicit edges) while ESLint reads import statements (seeing only explicit edges), so codependix gates at least as much and sometimes more.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://configuration/codependix.config.ts#L126-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b1dc1d565f3bab39c7a1d5341b3d5c1e67a7c265c7fdf151a7316497c5f8498:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d753cb086e674971933640220bee0c80",
      "statement": "Core vocabulary is strictly defined: Graph (one level built by one package), Neighborhood (project's one-hop deps/dependents), Workspace Graph (whole-repo graph exported once), Export (descriptive JSON/Markdown, never breached), Boundary (prescriptive allow/forbid/acyclic rules producing violations), Anchor (codependix-owned comment markers independent of conformetry).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTEXT.md#L249-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1b15091d069f7a793a650160bab859266beb59c9ac8179704b18a8338bd6d9f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65335c030227430b8e68c1fe5c17047f",
      "statement": "A boundary selector with no fields (id, path, project, tags) is refused rather than interpreted as matching every node, preventing typos from becoming workspace-wide rules.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://projects/ic-suite/codependix/codependix-configuration/src/modules/configuration/configuration-boundaries.types.ts#L115-L138",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b34d6d6a67c12feda7d4225c77354a4febe2a55910992be3c5af1c11f5d01731:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7bc38db5c70144588827563cdd41eafa",
      "statement": "A graph level with no declared rules is never built at all — judging NestJS requires booting containers, judging TypeScript requires building ts.Program — so a workspace declaring only Nx rules pays for neither.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://projects/ic-suite/codependix/codependix-boundaries/src/modules/boundary-check/boundary-check.service.ts#L37-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6b98b2059feea4bb0330a570a233a76870b60eb372307b520f0194b203311ee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_317d0b40daca410fa45ea0c03f9391c7",
      "statement": "Anchor renaming requires a two-place coordinated commit: rename in projectDefaults and re-splice every README in the same commit; a half-done rename leaves orphaned blocks that fail markdown-lint in the version commit's prepare hook, blocking the release.",
